cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GenomeX: unified genome QC — completeness, contamination, and comparative gene content"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it together with the underlying tools."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Hasnat-GPU
    name-particle: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hasnat-GPU/GenomeX"
abstract: >-
  GenomeX runs Prodigal, HMMER against BUSCO OrthoDB v10 profiles, MMseqs2 and
  fastANI in a single pass over bacterial assemblies, and joins their outputs
  into one report. It scores assembly completeness, detects cross-contamination
  from tetranucleotide composition, GC, displaced single-copy markers and
  compositional bimodality, distinguishes plasmids and secondary chromosomes
  from contaminants, and partitions strain-unique genes between contamination
  artefact, genomic-island acquisition and divergence — testing island
  clustering against a permutation null before calling it acquisition.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - genome-assembly
  - quality-control
  - contamination-detection
  - comparative-genomics
  - pangenome
  - average-nucleotide-identity
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-18"
